@startuml
title P1 macOS normal recording and self-test ownership

actor User
participant Shell
participant Workflow
participant Output
participant Capture
database Store

== Normal recording ==
User -> Shell : Record button or registered hotkey
Shell -> Workflow : toggleNormalRecording()
Workflow -> Capture : begin(selected input, explicit action)
Capture --> Workflow : playStartCue
Workflow -> Output : play reviewed cue
Output --> Workflow : completed
Workflow -> Capture : startCueCompleted()
Capture --> Shell : recording + scalar meter
User -> Shell : Stop
Shell -> Workflow : toggleNormalRecording()
Workflow -> Capture : stop()
Capture -> Store : finalize durable unsent draft
Capture --> Workflow : playStopCue + finished(draft)
Workflow -> Output : play reviewed cue
Output --> Workflow : completed
Workflow --> Shell : draft ready + idle

== Exact local self-test ==
User -> Shell : Record 5 seconds
Shell -> Workflow : recordFiveSeconds()
Workflow -> Capture : begin(explicit action)
Capture --> Workflow : start cue event
Workflow -> Output : cue
Output --> Workflow : completed
Workflow -> Capture : commit exactly 5 seconds
Capture -> Store : finalize completed draft
Workflow -> Output : stop cue, then completed draft
Output --> Shell : reviewing draft
User -> Shell : close or delete
Shell -> Workflow : closeSelfTest/deleteLocalDraft
Workflow -> Store : delete owned self-test media

note over Workflow,Store
Normal and self-test capture cannot overlap.
No upload or network call occurs in either local sequence.
end note
@enduml
